# Unraid's dated copies of the share `pbs` (unraid/undo.sh): each <date>/ is the whole datastore as
# it was that night, to put back what PBS lost (runbooks/restore.md, case 7). Unraid exports it
# read-only to 10.10.20.40, so not even root here can change a copy. soft: a read fails, rather
# than hangs, if Unraid goes away mid-restore.
[Unit]
Description=Unraid's copies of the PBS datastore (share undo-pbs), read-only

[Mount]
What=10.10.20.20:/mnt/user/undo-pbs
Where=/mnt/undo
Type=nfs
Options=ro,soft
